Noah-MP leaf-visibility exposure patch (adjudicated 2026-07-24, commit 3377df1)
==============================================================================

Target     : WRF v4.6.1 @ d66e442fccc04111067e29274c9f9eaccc3cef28
File       : phys/module_sf_noahmplsm.F
Pristine   : sha256 bd592a5b7db29000e715250e3a7c779ffb5e0dcc356f6b5a7d9e1c9f69c55282
Patched    : sha256 3cd3690d6455cfb8549cb41979b7e101e7436464c478f7f7973ab226488ac206
Lines      : 12351 before, 12351 after (one-for-one line substitution)
Statements : all 50 module accessibility statements at source lines 30-84

What this changes
-----------------
Every "private ::" accessibility *statement* becomes "public ::". Nothing
else. No declaration attribute, no executable statement, no expression, no
declaration order, and no line count changes.

The three "INTEGER, PRIVATE, PARAMETER" entity-attribute declarations
(MBAND at line 222, NSOIL at 223, NSTAGE at 224) are deliberately NOT
touched: those are attribute specifications inside a type declaration, not
accessibility statements, so the module's own private constants stay private
and cannot leak into a harness program unit.

Lifted symbols, in source order (the exact set the harness re-verifies):

  ATM PHENOLOGY PRECIP_HEAT ENERGY THERMOPROP CSNOW TDFCND RADIATION ALBEDO
  SNOW_AGE SNOWALB_BATS SNOWALB_CLASS GROUNDALB TWOSTREAM SURRAD VEGE_FLUX
  SFCDIF1 SFCDIF2 STOMATA CANRES ESAT RAGRB BARE_FLUX TSNOSOI HRT HSTEP
  ROSR12 PHASECHANGE FRH2O WATER CANWATER SNOWWATER SNOWFALL COMBINE DIVIDE
  COMBO COMPACT SNOWH2O SOILWATER ZWTEQ INFIL SRT WDFCND1 WDFCND2 SSTEP
  GROUNDWATER SHALLOWWATERTABLE CARBON CO2FLUX ERROR

The two commented-out entries (BVOCFLUX at line 81, CH4FLUX at line 82) are
comments and are left as comments; they name routines that do not exist in
v4.6.1.

Why
---
MODULE_SF_NOAHMPLSM exports exactly two procedures, NOAHMP_SFLX and
noahmp_options. Every solver leaf is private, so a per-leaf oracle against
the byte-unmodified module is impossible. Two alternatives were adjudicated
and rejected:

  * whole-column-only oracles: a mismatch localises to "somewhere in a
    9,300-line column", which is not a debuggable signal;
  * BIND(C, name="__module_sf_noahmplsm_MOD_<leaf>") symbol aliasing: UNSAFE,
    not merely fragile. The built module already exposes IPA-renamed
    specialisations such as "..._MOD_sfcdif1.constprop.0.isra.0", so an alias
    can silently bind a specialised clone instead of the real routine and
    yield a passing oracle for the wrong function.

Visibility is not physics. private/public cannot change numerical semantics,
and at the harness's -O0 it cannot change the codegen of the routine bodies
at all.

Audit
-----
tools/noahmp_wrf461_oracle/check_visibility_patch.py re-derives the patched
file from the pristine one, asserts both SHA-256 digests above, asserts the
two files have identical line counts, and asserts that every differing line
is exactly a "private ::" -> "public ::" substitution with the symbol name
and all surrounding whitespace preserved. build_leaves.sh runs it before
compiling and fails closed.

The pristine whole-column harness (build.sh / run_sflx.F90) keeps compiling
the UNPATCHED module, so gpuwm/data/noahmp/oracle/noahmp-sflx.csv remains a
byte-unmodified reference and stays available as the composition cross-check.

